Confident hinge loss introduces a margin-based mechanism that penalizes incorrect classifications when the model’s prediction is too close to the correct class, thus forcing the model to increase its confidence in the correct class. The loss function is designed to ensure that the correct class has a higher probability than any incorrect class by a fixed margin. This prevents the model from assigning high confidence to incorrect predictions, improving the overall classification performance. The confident hinge loss is defined as shown in Eq. (3):3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
