The performance of the model is evaluated based on five metrics: sensitivity (Sn), specificity (Sp), accuracy (Acc), Matthews correlation coefficient (MCC) and the area under the ROC curve. The closer these values are to 1, the better the model’s performance. The formulas for calculating these four metrics are provided in Eq. (4), The area under the ROC curve was calculated using the SK-Learn metrics package.\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
